> A calculation before fitting

At the origin, a unit independent bivariate normal has density1/(2*pi). Multiplying by a fair Bernoulli pen event gives1/(4*pi), so this simple offset/pen negative log likelihood is log(4*pi). The fitted model uses a conditional three-component mixture.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/handwriting_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;double computed=-n::log(n::scalar(1./(4*std::numbers::pi),n::DType::Float64)).item(),analytic=std::log(4*std::numbers::pi);if(std::abs(computed-analytic)>2e-6)throw std::runtime_error("hand calculation differs from native primitives");std::print("| native calculation | analytic reference |\n|---:|---:|\n| {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",computed,analytic);dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(std::vector<double>{0,1},std::vector<double>{computed,analytic},"worked reference",{37,99,235}).ylim(0,std::max(.5,std::max(computed,analytic)*1.2)).x_label("0 = native calculation;1 = analytic reference").y_label("Toy objective or diagnostic value").title("handwriting hand calculation").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/handwriting_worked.svg");}
```
